# Named Tables: Error Cases
# Each section demonstrates an error that should produce a diagnostic.

## Undefined table reference

x = missing_table.col

---

## Undefined column reference

<!-- table: data (a, b) -->
| A  | B  |
|----|-----|
| 10 | 20 |

---

x = data.nonexistent

---

## Column count mismatch (directive says 2, table has 3)

<!-- table: wrong (x, y) -->
| A  | B  | C  |
|----|----|----|
| 1  | 2  | 3  |

---

## Mixed types in a column

<!-- table: mixed (val) -->
| Value |
|-------|
| $100  |
| 50%   |

---

## Element-wise length mismatch

<!-- table: short (a) -->
| A |
|---|
| 1 |
| 2 |

---

<!-- table: long (b) -->
| B |
|---|
| 1 |
| 2 |
| 3 |

---

bad = short.a + long.b

---

## Duplicate table name

<!-- table: dup (x) -->
| X |
|---|
| 1 |

---

<!-- table: dup (y) -->
| Y |
|---|
| 2 |

---

## Empty cell in table

<!-- table: gaps (a, b) -->
| A  | B  |
|----|-----|
| 10 |    |
| 20 | 30 |

---

## Dot access on non-table variable

scalar = 42

---

x = scalar.field

---

## Mixed array and scalar in sum

<!-- table: nums (v) -->
| V |
|---|
| 1 |
| 2 |

---

bad_sum = sum(nums.v, 10)

---

## Nested dot access

<!-- table: t (a) -->
| A |
|---|
| 1 |

---

bad = t.a.something
